# Dev Notes 20 — Runtime Layout Config/Profile Helper Unit

This note records the follow-up config/profile helper layout unit for `runtime-layout-folder-structure-v1`.

## Purpose

Move config and retry/profile helper modules under `runtime/config/` after the parent runtime internals had already been moved under `runtime/` subfolders.

This change is layout-only. It does not redesign config override validation, retry/profile planning, context retry behavior, hardware probing, runtime scheduling, worker lifecycle, prompt/output semantics, model identity/path behavior, or worker protocol messages.

## Public entrypoint and worker boundary

`runtime.mjs` remains the canonical public runtime entrypoint at the repo root.

These path-sensitive files remain at the repo root:

```text
runtime.mjs
workerBridge.mjs
llama_worker/llama.mjs
```

`workerBridge.mjs` still constructs the worker from `./llama_worker/llama.mjs`.

`llama_worker/llama.mjs` still resolves `modelPath` from the worker file location and `config.modelLoad.baseModel`. The import path for config changed, but model path semantics did not.

## Moved config/profile helper modules

```text
config.mjs               -> runtime/config/config.mjs
configOverride.mjs       -> runtime/config/configOverride.mjs
contextRetryProfiles.mjs -> runtime/config/contextRetryProfiles.mjs
hardwareProbe.mjs        -> runtime/config/hardwareProbe.mjs
retryProfiles.mjs        -> runtime/config/retryProfiles.mjs
```

## Import propagation

Imports were updated in:

```text
runtime.mjs
llama_worker/llama.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/nativeOperationPolicy.mjs
runtime/lifecycle/runtimeInitCoordinator.mjs
runtime/config/retryProfiles.mjs
tests/* direct helper imports
tests/* fixture-copy RUNTIME_FILES lists
tests/* temporary config patch paths
```

## Behavior boundaries preserved

This unit preserves:

```text
config as the primary tuning surface
validated configOverride surface
modelLoad.baseModel non-overrideability
worker as native/model execution boundary
parent runtime ownership of request lifecycle
retry/profile planning behavior
context retry behavior
hardware probe behavior
workerBridge generation guard behavior
init/reset/shutdown behavior
prompt/output semantics
```

## Verification focus

Because this unit touches config imports used by both parent and worker code, verification should include the full mock/sandbox smoke set:

```bash
find . -name '*.mjs' -print0 | sort -z | xargs -0 -n1 node --check
grep -R "inference\.mjs" -n --include='*.mjs' .
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestNativeOperationHardStopPolicy.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerOperationSerialization.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestContextCreationRetry.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestContextCreationCancelBoundary.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestWorkerNativeCancellationBoundary.mjs
SKIP_REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestDrainShutdown.mjs
SKIP_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestHardwareAwareInitRetry.mjs
```

Before upload or merge-readiness, Michael-side real-runtime checks should still be run from the final candidate directory because both parent and worker import paths changed.
